    {
      "math_academy_id": "q-8690",
      "knowledge_point_id": "26666440-d376-5cb6-b922-9850e5c42eb3",
      "knowledge_point": "Solving a Trigonometric Equation Involving Cosine Under a Modified Domain",
      "problem": "Given that ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ are the solutions of the equation $\\operatorname{cos}⁡x=-\\frac{1}{6}$ for $-\\pi <x\\le \\pi ,$ what is the value of ${x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2}$ rounded to the nearest integer?",
      "worked_solution": "First, we find the principal value:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x=\\operatorname{arccos}⁡(-\\frac{1}{6})=1.738\\,244…≈1.738\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $1.738$ lies inside the given domain, our first solution is ${x}_{1}=1.738.$\n\nOur first solution lies in the second quadrant and has a reference angle of \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\theta }_{R}=\\pi -1.738 & ≈1.404.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $\\operatorname{cos}⁡x<0,$ the second solution must lie in the third quadrant, and it also has a reference angle ${\\theta }_{R}=1.404.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13968930/assets/392ae25b9a2aa47e5292d7e623922803891b52099d20525f888daca92642ce88.png)\n\nA second solution $X$ lies in the $3$rd quadrant, and we can find it using the reference angle, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}X & =\\pi +{\\theta }_{R} \\\\  & =\\pi +1.404 \\\\  & =4.546\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHowever, this value is not in the required domain. To get a second solution that's within the required domain, we simply subtract $2\\pi $ from $X:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{2} & =X-2\\pi  \\\\  & =4.546-2\\pi  \\\\  & ≈-1.738\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally,\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}{x}_{2}≈1.738\\cdot (-1.738)≈-3\n$$\n\nrounded to the nearest integer.",
